{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/61098-angels-and-gadgets-on-the-job","id":61098,"title":"Angels and Gadgets on the job","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Demon: The Descent"],"posts":[{"date":"2014-01-29T15:07:57-08:00","id":61098,"title":"Angels and Gadgets on the job","content":"Do angels ever use the equivalent of Gadgets?<br /> <br /> Are they like, gonna have a special 'Unchained Tazer' or something?<br /> <br /> Or do they prefer to use regular tazers?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/762-missmaddy","name":"MissMaddy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar762_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"380"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-29T17:14:45-08:00","id":61177,"title":"","content":"Pretty sure that Gadgets are an excellent example of demons having to learn how to stretch out their abilities in ways that loyalists don't have to or really understand how to.<br /> <br /> If an angel decides to go with a taser, then it's probably built into their angelic form, or they use an electric shock Numina. I suppose they could also go with a mundane taser if they have to improvise.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Mage the Awakening 2e Communal Homebrew Threads:<br /> - <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/966394-perils-of-the-path-post-your-homebrew\" target=\"_blank\">Perils of the Path</a> - Other homebrew threads linked in the OP!<br /> <br /> Join us at the unofficial IRC channels on.irc.sorcery.net at #exalted and now #theonyxpath!","edited":{"userid":451,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/451-kirby-jerusalem","user":"Kirby Jerusalem","date":". 01-29-2014, 08:20 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/451-kirby-jerusalem","name":"Kirby Jerusalem","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar451_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"589"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-29T19:09:04-08:00","id":61243,"title":"","content":"My understanding is that angels come outfitted with the tools to complete their missions. Barring those instances where for some inexplicable reason the G-M sets angels up for failure and thus precipitates or assists in their fall.<br /> <br /> So if an angel required a taser for their mission they would probably have some kind of internal/angelic form taser. Electro-whip tail, tesla-coils jutting out of their shoulders, or such ilk.<br /> <br /> I think it COULD be possible for SOME angels to have mission parameters that have enough latitude or lee-way which would force/allow them to improvise. However, I think gadgets as presented are the hall-mark of demon ingenuity and an new expression to their aether-fuelled existence. <br /> <br /> So I'm suggesting that perhaps a Messenger whose mission did not include combat or self-defence would pick up and use a regular taser if it had to. However I think that sitting down and bodging together some kind of essence fuelled device to incapacitate potential hostiles would be so unlikely as to warrant immediate recall and repair if the G-M or its agents were alerted to that fact. I think it would be an interesting NPC/potential ally/PC origin story.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1930-rixx","name":"Rixx","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1930_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"34"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}